<div class="flex flex-col gap-3 animate-appear text-sm leading-relaxed text-center md:text-left">
  <p>
    I'm an undergraduate researcher at NYU's Center for Data Science, part of the Courant
    Institute, studying Data Science with a minor in Philosophy.
  </p>
  <p>
    My work is machine learning on nervous systems and the people who have them: decoding
    handwriting from wrist EMG on Meta's open sEMG benchmark, where I reproduced Meta's
    released models and then halved their error with personalization and a language model
    (30.1% → 15.0% character error); decoding speech from MEG; modeling whole-brain activity
    in <em>C. elegans</em>; and the genetics behind migraine, hypermobility, autism and
    vascular dementia. Most projects ship with an interactive demo you can run in the browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    I build the experiment, then I try to break it, and I publish both. Every headline number
    on this site has been through a leakage audit, and the ones that didn't survive are marked.
  </p>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    Underneath it all is one question I keep circling from different sides: what a mind is.
  </p>
  <p class="pt-1">
    More on <a href="/projects" class="underline hover:font-bold">Projects</a>
    and the <a href="/posts" class="underline hover:font-bold">Blog</a>.
  </p>
